From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: poll ADM_STAT/MSDU_COUNT when NPU offload is active

mt7996_mac_work() requests the per-wcid ALL_STA_INFO ADM_STAT (tx/rx
bytes) and MSDU_COUNT (tx/rx packets) tags only while a WED device is
active, on the reasoning that without hardware offload mac80211's own
software counters are authoritative and the firmware poll is redundant.

Airoha NPU offload bypasses the host exactly the way WED does: forwarded
frames never traverse mac80211, so its software counters stall while the
firmware keeps counting at the MAC. On an NPU board the gate leaves
wcid->stats.{tx,rx}_bytes and {tx,rx}_packets permanently at zero (the
unconditional TXRX_RATE poll is why the per-link rate still updates).

Extend the gate with mt76_npu_device_active() so NPU builds collect the
same firmware counters WED builds do. Two extra MCU queries per stats
cycle, only when the NPU is actually attached.

Signed-off-by: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2996,7 +2996,8 @@
 		mt7996_mac_update_stats(phy);
 
 		mt7996_mcu_get_all_sta_info(phy, UNI_ALL_STA_TXRX_RATE);
-		if (mtk_wed_device_active(&phy->dev->mt76.mmio.wed)) {
+		if (mtk_wed_device_active(&phy->dev->mt76.mmio.wed) ||
+		    mt76_npu_device_active(&phy->dev->mt76)) {
 			mt7996_mcu_get_all_sta_info(phy, UNI_ALL_STA_TXRX_ADM_STAT);
 			mt7996_mcu_get_all_sta_info(phy, UNI_ALL_STA_TXRX_MSDU_COUNT);
 		}
